===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# {{lb|en|of|distance or position; also figurative}} Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.
## [[extend|Extending]] [[far]] [[down]] from the [[top]], or [[surface]], to the [[bottom]], literally or figuratively.
##: {{ux|en|The lake is extremely '''deep'''.}}
##: {{ux|en|We hiked into a '''deep''' valley between tall mountains.}}
##: {{ux|en|There was a '''deep''' layer of dust on the floor; the room had not been disturbed for many years.}}
##: {{ux|en|In the mid-1970s, the economy went into a '''deep''' recession.}}
##: {{ux|en|We are in '''deep''' trouble.}}
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 6-2|III|i|130|2|Smooth runnes the Water, where the Brooke is '''deepe''',}}
##* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=5|passage=Here, in the transept and choir, where the service was being held, one was conscious every moment of an increasing brightness; colours glowing vividly beneath the circular chandeliers, and the rows of small lights on the choristers' desks flashed and sparkled in front of the boys' faces, '''deep''' linen collars, and red neckbands.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=September 28 2013|author=w:Kenan Malik|title=London Is Special, but Not That Special|titleurl=http://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/29/opinion/sunday/london-is-special-but-not-that-special.html?ref=opinion|journal=New York Times|accessdate=28 September 2013
|passage=While Britain’s recession has been '''deep''' and unforgiving, in London it has been relatively shallow.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=11-07-2015|author=|title=Antimicrobial Photoinactivation Using Visible Light Plus Water-Filtered Infrared-A (VIS + wIRA) Alters In Situ Oral Biofilms|journal=PLOS ONE|url=http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0132107|doi=10.1371/journal.pone.0132107|volume=|issue=|pages=
|passage=The differences in biofilm penetration patterns of both tested photosensitisers and the light source could have played an important role for the survival of microorganisms after the application of aPDT. In a recent own study, we showed that the '''deepest''' layers of the oral biofilm were not affected by the aPDT [4 ].}}
## Positioned far from the surface or other reference point, especially down through something or into something.
##: {{ux|en|Diving down to '''deep''' wrecks can be dangerous.}}
##: {{ux|en|I can't get the bullet out – it's too '''deep'''.}}
## Far in [[extent]] in another (non-downwards, but generally also non-upwards) direction, especially front-to-back.
##: {{ux|en|The shelves are 30 centimetres '''deep'''. — They are '''deep''' shelves.}}
##: {{ux|en|That cyclist's '''deep''' chest allows him to draw more air.}}
## {{lb|en|in combination}} Extending to a level or length equivalent to the stated thing.
##: {{ux|en|The water was waist-'''deep'''.}}
##: {{ux|en|There is an arm-'''deep''' hole in the wall.}}
## In a (specified) number of [[rows]] or [[layers]].
##: {{ux|en|a crowd three '''deep''' along the funeral procession}}
## [[voluminous|Voluminous]].
##: {{ux|en|to take a '''deep''' breath / sigh / drink}}
##* {{RQ:Hough Purchase Price|chapter=I
|passage=Serene, smiling, enigmatic, she faced him with no fear whatever showing in her dark eyes.{{...}}She put back a truant curl from her forehead where it had sought egress to the world, and looked him full in the face now, drawing a '''deep''' breath which caused the round of her bosom to lift the lace at her throat.}}
## {{lb|en|cricket|baseball|softball}} Far from the center of the playing area, near to the [[boundary]] of the playing area, either in absolute terms or relative to a point of reference.
##: {{ux|en|He is fielding at '''deep''' mid wicket.}}
##: {{ux|en|She hit a ball into '''deep''' center field.}}
## {{lb|en|sports|_|such as|_|soccer|tennis}} Penetrating a long way, especially a long way forward.
##: {{ux|en|a '''deep''' volley}}
##: {{ux|en|a '''deep''' run into the opposition half}}
## {{lb|en|sports|_|such as|_|soccer|American football|tennis}} Positioned back, or [[downfield]], towards one's own goal, or towards or behind one's [[baseline]] or similar reference point.
##: {{ux|en|Our defensive live is too '''deep'''. We need to move further up the field.}}
##: {{ux|en|She returns serve from a very '''deep''' position.}}
## {{senseid|en|anatomy}} {{lb|en|anatomy|often with ''[[to]]''}} Further into the [[body]].
##: {{ant|en|superficial|id1=anatomy}}
##: {{ux|en|the brachialis is '''deep''' to the biceps}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|author=Dr. Melina Jampolis|title=The real science behind fascia ailments|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2018/11/08/health/fascia-blasting-explainer-exercise-jampolis/index.html|date=2018-11-08|passage=The superficial fascia surrounds the body and includes subcutaneous fat; the '''deep''' fascia surrounds the musculoskeletal system; the meningeal fascia surrounds the nervous system; the visceral fascia surrounds body cavities and organs.}}
# {{lb|en|intellectual|social}} Complex, involved.
## [[profound|Profound]], having [[great]] [[meaning]] or [[import]], but possibly [[obscure]] or not [[obvious]].
##: {{ux|en|That is a '''deep''' thought!}}
## [[significant|Significant]], not [[superficial]], in [[extent]].
##: {{ux|en|They're in '''deep''' discussion.}}
##* {{quote-song|en|year=1977|title={{w|How Deep Is Your Love (Bee Gees song)|How Deep is Your Love}}|artist=w:Bee Gees|passage=And it's me you need to show / How '''deep''' is your love?}}
## [[Hard]] to [[penetrate]] or [[comprehend]]; profound; [[intricate]]; [[obscure]].
##: {{ux|en|a '''deep''' subject or plot}}
##* {{circa|1840}}, {{w|Thomas De Quincey}}:
##*: Why it was that the ancients had no landscape painting, is a question '''deep''' almost as the mystery of life, and harder of solution than all the problems of jurisprudence combined.
## Of [[penetrating]] or [[far-reaching]] [[intellect]]; not superficial; [[thoroughly]] [[skilled]]; [[sagacious]]; [[cunning]].
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Pericles|act=V|scene=i|page=62|passage='''Deepe''' clearks ſhe dumb's}}
##* {{quote-song
|en
|title=I Never Said I Was Deep
|year=2009
|author=Jarvis Cocker
|album=Further Complications.
|passage=I never said I was '''deep''', but I am profoundly shallow / My lack of knowledge is vast, and my horizons are narrow}}
## [[inner|Inner]], [[underlying]], [[true]]; [[relating]] to one’s [[inner]] or [[private]] [[being]] rather than what is [[visible]] on the [[surface]].
##* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XVI|26|Or doth she only seem to take<br>⁠The touch of change in calm or storm;<br>⁠But knows no more of transient form<br>In her '''deep''' self, than some dead lake<br>That holds the shadow of a lark<br>⁠Hung in the shadow of a heaven?}}
# {{lb|en|sound|voice}} Low in [[pitch]].
#: {{ux|en|She has a very '''deep''' [[contralto]] voice.}}
#* {{RQ:Travers Cuckoo in the Nest|chapter=5|passage=The departure was not unduly prolonged.{{...}}Within the door Mrs. Spoker hastily imparted to Mrs. Love a few final sentiments on the subject of Divine Intention in the disposition of buckets; farewells and last commiserations; a '''deep''', guttural instigation to the horse; and the wheels of the waggonette crunched heavily away into obscurity.}}
# {{lb|en|of a color or flavour}} [[highly|Highly]] [[saturated]]; [[rich]].
#: {{ux|en|That's a very '''deep''' shade of blue.}}
#: {{ux|en|The spices impart a '''deep''' flavour to the dish.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=8|passage=The day was cool and snappy for August, and the Rise all green with a lavish nature. Now we plunged into a '''deep''' shade with the boughs lacing each other overhead, and crossed dainty, rustic bridges over the cold trout-streams, the boards giving back the clatter of our horses' feet:{{nb...}}.}}
# {{lb|en|sleep}} [[sound|Sound]], [[heavy]] (''describing a state of sleep from which one is not easily awoken'').
#: {{ux|en|He was in a '''deep''' sleep.}}
# [[muddy|Muddy]]; [[boggy]]; [[sandy]]; said of [[road]]s.
#* {{RQ:Clarendon History
|passage=The ways in that vale were very '''deep'''.}}
# {{lb|en|of time}} [[distant|Distant]] in the past, [[ancient]].
#: {{ux|en|'''deep''' time}}
#: {{ux|en|in the '''deep''' past}}

